  "reviewPolicy": "Recheck version behavior and feature availability with every seasonal release. Sources support the technical facts; SAM authored the scenarios and answer options. All 90 families and 30 semantic variants were reviewed for plausible technical distractors on 2026-11-09; incorrect options target real misconceptions and include specific feedback.",
  "versionCaveats": [
    {
      "topic": "Apex API 67.0",
      "note": "At Apex API 67.0, database operations default to user mode; at 66.0 and earlier they default to system mode. A class without a sharing keyword defaults to with sharing at 67.0. Before 67.0, omitting the keyword preserves the current sharing context, rather than universally meaning without sharing. WITH SECURITY_ENFORCED is unsupported from 67.0.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/apex-ref/references/apex-ref/versioned-behavior-changes.html"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Explicit access mode",
      "note": "WITH USER_MODE applies sharing and CRUD/FLS even inside a without sharing class. In system mode, record sharing depends on the class keyword; system mode is not automatically equivalent to without sharing.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/apex-dev/references/apex-dev/apex-classes-enforce-usermode.html"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Manual shares and API 68",
      "note": "Preservation of Manual shares during an ownership transfer depends on Keep Manual Shares when Transferring Records. Sharing reasons for supported standard objects are available from Metadata API 68.0; this does not cover master-detail children without a share object.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api-metadata/references/meta-types/metadata-sharingreason.html",
      "additionalSourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/blogs/2026/10/protect-apex-shares-custom-row-causes-on-standard-objects"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Restriction rules",
      "note": "Restriction rules apply only to supported objects and contexts. They narrow existing access rather than granting new access. Design user criteria so that one active rule applies to each user; two matching rules do not guarantee AND composition.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=platform.security_restriction_rule.htm&language=en_US&type=5"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Deferred sharing rules",
      "note": "The feature must be available in the org. After Resume, run a full Recalculate for accumulated changes. The pause does not stop every sharing mechanism, including manual shares.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=platform.security_sharing_rule_recalculation.htm&language=en_US&type=5"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Platform Events",
      "note": "Standard Platform Event and CDC retention is 72 hours. Replay ID is opaque and is not a universally unique identifier. Publish After Commit depends on a successful commit; Publish Immediately can precede commit or survive rollback. A successful publication SaveResult does not confirm subscriber processing.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
      "additionalSourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-publish-callbacks.html"
    },
    {
      "topic": "LWC",
      "note": "Do not assume a fixed Apex cache TTL. refreshApex takes the value emitted by the Apex wire; notifyRecordUpdateAvailable refreshes LDS knowledge of records changed through Apex. @track does not observe internal Date, Set, or Map mutations.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/lwc/guide/apex-result-caching.html",
      "additionalSourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/lwc/guide/reactivity-fields.html"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Omni-Channel",
      "note": "Standard Omni-Channel retired in Summer '26. Verify current labs against Enhanced Omni-Channel.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=sf.omnichannel_std_vs_enhanced.htm&language=en_US&type=5"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Agentforce",
      "note": "As of the review date, the referenced documentation supports agent testing in sandboxes and warns that tests can change data. Data 360 queries during tests can consume credits.",
      "sourceUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/ai/agentforce/guide/testing-api-get-started.html"
    }
  ],
